ground_truth:
`userInput` is declared inside `onAccept`, so a new empty list is created every time an item is accepted. Store it as a field in your widget’s `State` instead.

```dart
class _MyWidgetState extends State<MyWidget> {
  final List<Box> userInput = <Box>[];

  Widget _generateOpaque(int index) {
    return DragTarget<Box>(
      builder: (
        BuildContext context,
        List<Box?> accepted,
        List<dynamic> rejected,
      ) {
        return opaqueBoxes[index].filled
            ? _filledBox(index)
            : _opaqueBox(index);
      },
      onWillAccept: (Box? data) => data != null,
      onAccept: (Box data) {
        setState(() {
          userInput.add(data);
        });

        print(userInput.length);
      },
    );
  }
}
```

Use `setState` if the UI depends on `userInput`; otherwise, adding to the list does not require it. Also ensure `userInput` is not declared inside `build()` or `_generateOpaque()`, because those methods may run repeatedly.

Final answer: Move `userInput` to a field of the widget’s `State` and only call `userInput.add(data)` inside `onAccept`; currently you recreate the list on every drop.

