The strategy below records the coordinate at which each newly refilled bucket starts being used. After that coordinate, the bucket consumes up to `capacity` water units in row-major order. Thus, a strategy entry does not represent every individual water unit.

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Objects;

class Solution {

    /**
     * Minimal generic Pair implementation, avoiding dependencies such as
     * javafx.util.Pair.
     */
    public static final class Pair<K, V> {
        private final K key;
        private final V value;

        public Pair(K key, V value) {
            this.key = key;
            this.value = value;
        }

        public K getKey() {
            return key;
        }

        public V getValue() {
            return value;
        }

        @Override
        public boolean equals(Object object) {
            if (this == object) {
                return true;
            }
            if (!(object instanceof Pair<?, ?>)) {
                return false;
            }

            Pair<?, ?> other = (Pair<?, ?>) object;
            return Objects.equals(key, other.key)
                    && Objects.equals(value, other.value);
        }

        @Override
        public int hashCode() {
            return Objects.hash(key, value);
        }

        @Override
        public String toString() {
            return "[" + key + "," + value + "]";
        }
    }

    /**
     * Returns:
     *   key   -> coordinates at which a refilled bucket starts being used
     *   value -> minimum number of refills
     *
     * Water units are processed in row-major order. Each refill handles at
     * most {@code capacity} water units, so the minimum number of refills is
     * ceil(numberOfOnes / capacity).
     *
     * Time complexity:  O(rows * columns)
     * Space complexity: O(ceil(numberOfOnes / capacity))
     */
    public Pair<List<Pair<Integer, Integer>>, Integer> optimalFillStrategy(
            List<List<Integer>> grid, int capacity) {

        validateInput(grid, capacity);

        List<Pair<Integer, Integer>> strategy = new ArrayList<>();

        int remainingCapacity = 0;

        for (int row = 0; row < grid.size(); row++) {
            List<Integer> currentRow = grid.get(row);

            for (int column = 0; column < currentRow.size(); column++) {
                if (currentRow.get(column) == 0) {
                    continue;
                }

                // The previous bucket is empty, so refill before processing
                // this water unit. This coordinate marks the new bucketful.
                if (remainingCapacity == 0) {
                    strategy.add(new Pair<>(row, column));
                    remainingCapacity = capacity;
                }

                remainingCapacity--;
            }
        }

        return new Pair<>(strategy, strategy.size());
    }

    private void validateInput(List<List<Integer>> grid, int capacity) {
        if (grid == null || grid.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Grid must not be null or empty.");
        }

        if (capacity < 1 || capacity > 10) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "Bucket capacity must be between 1 and 10.");
        }

        if (grid.size() > 100) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "The grid may contain at most 100 rows.");
        }

        if (grid.get(0) == null || grid.get(0).isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "Grid rows must not be null or empty.");
        }

        int width = grid.get(0).size();
        if (width > 100) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "The grid may contain at most 100 columns.");
        }

        for (int row = 0; row < grid.size(); row++) {
            List<Integer> currentRow = grid.get(row);

            if (currentRow == null || currentRow.size() != width) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                        "All grid rows must have the same non-zero width.");
            }

            for (Integer cell : currentRow) {
                if (cell == null || (cell != 0 && cell != 1)) {
                    throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                            "Each grid cell must contain either 0 or 1.");
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

If there are `W` water units, each refill can remove at most `capacity` units, giving the lower bound `ceil(W / capacity)`. The algorithm groups the water units into batches of exactly `capacity`, except possibly the last batch, so it attains that bound and is optimal.

