/// Emits cross-browser box-shadow declarations and a simple fallback.
///
/// @param {Color} $fallback-color
///   Color of the solid outline shown when `box-shadow` is unavailable.
/// @param {ArgList} $shadows
///   One or more shadows using CSS box-shadow order:
///   `<x-offset> <y-offset> <blur-radius> <spread-radius> <color> [inset]`.
///   Multiple arguments produce multiple, comma-separated shadows.
///
/// @example scss
///   .card {
///     @include custom-shadows(
///       #b7b7b7,
///       0 2px 6px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25),
///       0 8px 20px -4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15)
///     );
///   }
@mixin custom-shadows($fallback-color, $shadows...) {
  // Baseline fallback. Unsupported browsers retain this outline.
  // It does not affect the element's dimensions.
  outline: 1px solid $fallback-color;

  // Prefixes support older WebKit/Gecko implementations.
  -webkit-box-shadow: $shadows;
  -moz-box-shadow: $shadows;
  box-shadow: $shadows;

  // Remove the fallback when feature queries confirm shadow support.
  @supports (box-shadow: 0 0 1px #000) {
    outline: none;
  }
}

/// Applies a predefined shadow to any number of selectors.
///
/// This mixin should normally be called at the stylesheet's top level.
///
/// @param {ArgList} $selectors
///   One or more selectors to which the default shadow is applied.
///
/// @example scss
///   @include shadow-elements(".card", ".dialog", ".dropdown");
@mixin shadow-elements($selectors...) {
  @each $selector in $selectors {
    #{$selector} {
      @include custom-shadows(
        #b7b7b7,
        0 3px 8px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.24)
      );
    }
  }
}

// Example:
@include shadow-elements(".card", ".modal", ".menu");

.featured-card {
  @include custom-shadows(
    #999,
    2px 4px 10px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.30),
    0 0 4px 0 rgba(40, 100, 255, 0.25) inset
  );
}
```

The fallback is an outline rather than a simulated blur because unsupported browsers cannot reproduce a true box shadow. It remains visible in older browsers that ignore both `box-shadow` and `@supports`, while supported browsers remove it.

Final answer: The SCSS above provides a multi-element shadow mixin, a variadic customizable shadow mixin, vendor-prefixed declarations, and a non-layout-affecting fallback.

