Social media companies should generally be able to moderate posts on their own platforms, but not without limits or accountability.

They should be allowed to remove illegal content, credible threats, targeted harassment, fraud, exploitation, and material that seriously undermines platform safety. They may also enforce clearly stated community standards, since compelling a private platform to publish everything can violate its own editorial and associational rights.

