public String makePalindrome(String string) {
    int length = string.length();
    int suffixStart = 0;

    // Find the longest suffix that is already a palindrome.
    for (; suffixStart < length; suffixStart++) {
        int left = suffixStart;
        int right = length - 1;

        while (left < right && string.charAt(left) == string.charAt(right)) {
            left++;
            right--;
        }

        if (left >= right) {
            break;
        }
    }

    StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder(length + suffixStart);
    result.append(string);

    // Append the reversed prefix preceding the palindromic suffix.
    for (int i = suffixStart - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        result.append(string.charAt(i));
    }

    return result.toString();
}
```

This takes \(O(n^2)\) time in the worst case and \(O(n)\) space for the result.

Final answer: The function above returns the shortest palindrome beginning with the supplied string.

