For example, the scores of `-1`, `-11`, `1`, `-12`, and `11` are respectively `-1`, `0`, `1`, `1`, and `2`. The equal-score values `1` and `-12` retain their original order.

```java
import java.util.List;

public class Solution {
    public int specialFilter(List<Integer> nums) {
        int count = 0;

        for (Integer value : nums) {
            if (value == null || value <= 10) {
                continue;
            }

            int lastDigit = value % 10;
            int firstDigit = value;

            while (firstDigit >= 10) {
                firstDigit /= 10;
            }

            if (firstDigit % 2 != 0 && lastDigit % 2 != 0) {
                count++;
            }
        }

        return count;
    }
}
