For \(i \bmod 3\):

- If \(i \equiv 2\), then \(i^2-i+1 \equiv 0 \pmod 3\).
- Otherwise, \(i^2-i+1 \equiv 1 \pmod 3\).

Since no array element has residue 2, a valid triple must contain either three residue-0 elements or three residue-1 elements.

```java
public class Solution {
    public int getMaxTriples(int n) {
        long countZero = (n + 1L) / 3; // Indices 2, 5, 8, ...
        long countOne = n - countZero;

        long result = chooseThree(countZero) + chooseThree(countOne);
        return Math.toIntExact(result);
    }

    private long chooseThree(long count) {
        if (count < 3) {
            return 0;
        }
        return count * (count - 1) * (count - 2) / 6;
    }
}
```

