The selector is scoped to actual `<button>` elements with the `submit` class. Using `:not(:disabled)` prevents hover and active styles from applying to disabled buttons. The mixins set only explicitly selected properties, avoiding resets, broad selectors, shorthands, and `!important`, so unrelated existing styles remain intact.

```scss
// _submit-button.scss

// Variables use !default so they can be overridden before this file is loaded.
$submit-background: #2563eb !default;
$submit-color: #ffffff !default;
$submit-border-color: #1d4ed8 !default;

$submit-hover-background: #1d4ed8 !default;
$submit-hover-color: $submit-color !default;
$submit-hover-border-color: #1e40af !default;

$submit-active-background: #1e40af !default;
$submit-active-color: $submit-color !default;
$submit-active-border-color: #1e3a8a !default;

$submit-disabled-background: #cbd5e1 !default;
$submit-disabled-color: #64748b !default;
$submit-disabled-border-color: #94a3b8 !default;
$submit-disabled-opacity: 0.65 !default;

// Only emits properties whose values are provided.
@mixin submit-state(
  $background: null,
  $color: null,
  $border-color: null
) {
  @if $background != null {
    background-color: $background;
  }

  @if $color != null {
    color: $color;
  }

  @if $border-color != null {
    border-color: $border-color;
  }
}

@mixin submit-button {
  @include submit-state(
    $submit-background,
    $submit-color,
    $submit-border-color
  );

  // Disabled buttons cannot receive hover or active styling.
  &:not(:disabled) {
    &:hover {
      @include submit-state(
        $submit-hover-background,
        $submit-hover-color,
        $submit-hover-border-color
      );
    }

    // Placed after hover so active wins when both states match.
    &:active {
      @include submit-state(
        $submit-active-background,
        $submit-active-color,
        $submit-active-border-color
      );
    }
  }

  &:disabled {
    @include submit-state(
      $submit-disabled-background,
      $submit-disabled-color,
      $submit-disabled-border-color
    );

    cursor: not-allowed;
    opacity: $submit-disabled-opacity;
  }
}

// Applies only to <button class="submit"> elements.
button.submit {
  @include submit-button;
}
```

This deliberately avoids properties such as `all`, `outline`, `font`, `border`, or `transition`, which could reset unrelated existing button or focus styles.

Final answer: The SCSS above scopes base, hover, active, and disabled styling to `button.submit` while preserving unrelated existing styles.

