Ministry of Sound grew by turning a disused bus garage in Elephant and Castle, south London, into a club designed around the music rather than conventional nightlife. Opened in 1991 by James Palumbo, Humphrey Waterhouse and DJ Justin Berkmann, it drew inspiration from New York’s Paradise Garage and distinguished itself through:

