This occurred mainly during periods of forced conversion—especially under the Almohads in the 12th century—and was not the normal condition of Moroccan Jewry. Jews who remained and outwardly accepted Islam were known in Jewish tradition as **anusim** (“the coerced”). Some maintained Judaism secretly by:

